{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions","id":38158,"title":"Seeking some Birthright suggestions....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-27T21:36:57-08:00","id":38158,"title":"Seeking some Birthright suggestions....","content":"Okay, so my friends and I are preparing for our newest Scion game and we just had our first preliminary meeting to select pantheons, divine parents, and Purview specialties. Two of my players are seeking advice on possible Birthrights for their Scions.<br /> <br /> The first Scion is a Scion of Ishtar. We are using Gotham By Night's systems for this game, for the record. Now this player needs the most help, since unfortunately none of us are too familiar with Ancient Babylon. What kind of relics are most appropriate for Annuna Scions? What are some signature Babylonian relics, weapons, etc?<br /> <br /> To give you an idea about this character? He's about eighteen years old, and like Ishtar, he's focusing on his Social Attributes. He's a seductive type who likes to manipulate people. He's also capable in the Physical field as well, as our game will be fairly combat heavy. For his Purviews? Everyone selected four. His four specialties are Fire, Chaos, Health, and Illusion.<br /> <br /> What do you think are appropriate relics for such a character/power set?<br /> <br /> The second character isn't as bad off. The player has several relic ideas already, but two Purviews escape him right now. He's playing a Scion of Tsuki-Yomi. and the two Purviews with which he's having trouble are Psychopomp and Stars. What would be an appropriate relic(s) for a Japanese Scion with these two powers?<br /> <br /> Also, as we are using Gotham By Night's Stars Purview, he's already noticed that Boon they have where you can call down the constellations to aid you. Does anyone know any books and/or web sites that detail Japanese Astrology? Where can one find information on Japanese constellations?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T01:00:58-08:00","id":38195,"title":"","content":"For Babylon, you're looking at cylinder seals, cuneiform tablets and ceremonial headdresses. All very, very important to ancient Babylon. He's a man, and he's a manly man (seductive, yes?) so he <i>obviously</i> has a badass Babylon Beard, yes? He could easily invest in a Health Relic that takes the form of beard decorations. Seriously, beards and decorating them was a <i>big deal</i> in Babylonian society. Also, it looks badass. The Babylonians also loved them some bracelets, armbands and rings. They also used ceremonial weapons like maces, which always does a great job doubling as a phallic symbol. Sometimes Ishtar is represented as a winged woman, you might do something with his mom's feathers.<br /> <br /> I can't really offer much for the Kami player. Never been that interested in the Asian religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T06:26:45-08:00","id":38266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38195#post38195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Babylon, you're looking at cylinder seals, cuneiform tablets and ceremonial headdresses. All very, very important to ancient Babylon. He's a man, and he's a manly man (seductive, yes?) so he <i>obviously</i> has a badass Babylon Beard, yes? He could easily invest in a Health Relic that takes the form of beard decorations. Seriously, beards and decorating them was a <i>big deal</i> in Babylonian society. Also, it looks badass. The Babylonians also loved them some bracelets, armbands and rings. They also used ceremonial weapons like maces, which always does a great job doubling as a phallic symbol. Sometimes Ishtar is represented as a winged woman, you might do something with his mom's feathers.<br /> <br /> I can't really offer much for the Kami player. Never been that interested in the Asian religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that's a Hell of a good start. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I also did some more research at Gotham By Night and downloaded their Annuna download. Some pretty cool relic ideas in there. Yeah, the cylinder seals you mention were in there. Better start doing some research on those. I also found one mention of salmu, or sacred images. The idea of this guy having a statue of Ishtar somewhere in his possession could be kinda cool too. If you're not familiar, the download says it's a statue of one's divine parent, two to five feet tall. The cool thing is that you don't have to carry it around all the time. As long as it remains in your possession, you have access to two Purviews. If someone steals the thing out of your house, however? Big problems.<br /> <br /> So, okay, that's a good starting point for my Babylon research. Maces are an intriguing thought. Do you know where I can find some good images of Babylonian maces? I trust they don't look exactly like the Medieval maces that I'm thinking about right now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T07:22:38-08:00","id":38281,"title":"","content":"Exactly like Medieval maces, no. Generally the same shape, yes. In thousands of years, there hasn't been a lot of evolution in the most efficient way to crush someone's head with a heavy bit of metal. It's pretty easy to find some examples, though. A thorough Googling for &quot;Mesopotamian Mace&quot;, &quot;Babylonian Mace&quot;, &quot;Assyrian Mace&quot; and suchnot will get you some results. Here's a sample: <a href=\"http://www.christies.com/lotfinder/lot/a-mesopotamian-elamite-bronze-mace-head-late-3rd-3993833-details.aspx?intObjectID=3993833\" target=\"_blank\">Mesopotamian Mace at Christie's for Auction</a>.<br /> <br /> The art by TerriblyUncreative that went into the GBN Anunna supplement shows the beard ornaments of Mesopotamian men pretty well. If you watched The Hobbit, you saw the Dwarf King rocking some pretty snazzy beard-bling of his own. I don't mention the beard-bling just because it's cool, it shows up regularly in artistic depictions of powerful male figures. If you want Birthright ideas for an ancient culture, their art is the best place to go. Just try some brief image searches for Mesopotamian Art, or Babylonian Art. You'll get some great ideas very quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Don't miss checking out <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baghdad_Battery\" target=\"_blank\">Babylon Batteries</a>. Modern science says they're just boring old vessels for sacred texts, but <i>they could totally have been the first-ever electrochemical battery!!</i> Obviously, Scion goes with the cooler of the two ideas. Sounds like a good channel for Sky or Fire to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 12-28-2013, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T07:29:20-08:00","id":38284,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38281#post38281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly like Medieval maces, no. Generally the same shape, yes. In thousands of years, there hasn't been a lot of evolution in the most efficient way to crush someone's head with a heavy bit of metal. It's pretty easy to find some examples, though. A thorough Googling for &quot;Mesopotamian Mace&quot;, &quot;Babylonian Mace&quot;, &quot;Assyrian Mace&quot; and suchnot will get you some results. Here's a sample: <a href=\"http://www.christies.com/lotfinder/lot/a-mesopotamian-elamite-bronze-mace-head-late-3rd-3993833-details.aspx?intObjectID=3993833\" target=\"_blank\">Mesopotamian Mace at Christie's for Auction</a>.<br /> <br /> The art by TerriblyUncreative that went into the GBN Anunna supplement shows the beard ornaments of Mesopotamian men pretty well. If you watched The Hobbit, you saw the Dwarf King rocking some pretty snazzy beard-bling of his own. I don't mention the beard-bling just because it's cool, it shows up regularly in artistic depictions of powerful male figures. If you want Birthright ideas for an ancient culture, their art is the best place to go. Just try some brief image searches for Mesopotamian Art, or Babylonian Art. You'll get some great ideas very quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I did notice the beard decorations on GBN and as soon as you mentioned it, I began to realize just how often I had seen those kind of things. Yeah I also saw the Hobbit and I noticed the beard decorations there as well. Those actually ARE pretty badass-looking. It's up to my player if he wants to use those, but if this were my character? I'd take them in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> As for the ancient batteries? Hells yeah! I've been intrigued by those ever since I saw that Mythbusters episode when they worked on those. That was one of their earliest episodes, if you've never seen it. And as I recall, THEY were able to generate at least some electrical charge in their efforts to recreate the technology. So yeah, a Sky or Fire relic like that may be kinda cool too.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, I'm researching maces and Mesopotamian art. Thanks for the good ideas so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 12-28-2013, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T08:27:10-08:00","id":38293,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested to hear what your player ends up going with. Sorry I can't offer much for the Kami. As far as I know, the <i>Chinese</i> have a lot more focus on astrology and astronomy than the Japanese. I can't recall much in the way of Japanese star-mythology at all. Then again, I don't know all that much about Shinto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T09:17:24-08:00","id":38302,"title":"","content":"I cannot think of any specific relic associated with him, but Amatsu-Mikaboshi is the Kami of the Stars. Perhaps your player could look in that direction? You said you're using JSR rules, correct? In that case, none of the playable Kami have Stars associated, so Tsuki-Yomi would have to get it from somewhere else. It would be an interesting plot hook: how exactly did Tsuki-Yomi get a piece of Mikaboshi's power? Is he finally fed of up the fact that Amaterasu will just not let the Uke-Mochi incident go? And why did Mikaboshi agree to his part of the deal?<br /> <br /> Hope that helps, sorry I don't have any ideas for Psychoppomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T09:52:32-08:00","id":38320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38302#post38302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot think of any specific relic associated with him, but Amatsu-Mikaboshi is the Kami of the Stars. Perhaps your player could look in that direction? You said you're using JSR rules, correct? In that case, none of the playable Kami have Stars associated, so Tsuki-Yomi would have to get it from somewhere else. It would be an interesting plot hook: how exactly did Tsuki-Yomi get a piece of Mikaboshi's power? Is he finally fed of up the fact that Amaterasu will just not let the Uke-Mochi incident go? And why did Mikaboshi agree to his part of the deal?<br /> <br /> Hope that helps, sorry I don't have any ideas for Psychoppomp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we are using JSR rules, and yeah we did notice that none of the Kami have Stars. That was one of the reasons why my player wants Stars. Nice to be able to have a job that the established gods of the pantheon don't have yet.<br /> <br /> Your idea about the relic coming from Amatsu-Mikaboshi is very interesting. A big theme about this particular game is the concept of &quot;favors given and owed.&quot; So, yeah, I should give some thought as to how Tsuki-Yomi came by a Stars relic.<br /> <br /> I should point out that in this particular story? The Titan War hasn't actually started yet. It may not start at all. With this story, I'm going for more of a Percy Jackson kind of feel. The players are young Scions who attend special schools maintained by their respective pantheons. The game will actually begin with kind of a &quot;Tri-Wizard Cup Tournament&quot; kind of competition between their respective schools. Think &quot;Hunger Games&quot; but without the unwilling participants and the murder. The goal isn't to kill everyone else in the contest. It's more of a &quot;Capture the Flag&quot; kind of game. The gods create a challenging environment for the Scions, who have to locate some important object, get it, and return it successfully to their particular pantheon's camp. This allows for Scions of all stripes to have a decent shot at winning. Yeah, the combat monsters will just try to fight their way to victory, but the more cerebral Scions can try to win through brains over brawn and Social players can play the manipulation game to get what they want. Like Hunger Games, competing Scions can make or break alliances at will and it is understood that any alliances are temporary as there can only be one victor.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the players are actually starting out at Legend 5, using the rules found in the Scion: Companion. I want the competition to be challenging for the players, but I figured it was only fair that they have access to at least some of the more readily useful powers in order to keep things interesting. Also, like the Hunger Games, Scions can expect aid from the gods, much like Tributes could win aid from Sponsors. The Scion of Odin is running low on Legend? Poof! One of Idun's Golden Apples appears nearby him. The Scion of Horus is being pursued by the Scion of Zeus, in an attempt to capture the object from him and claim victory for the Theoi instead? Boom! A timely intervention from Geb raises an earthen wall to slow the Scion of Zeus down. That kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> So, with everyone starting out at Legend 5, perhaps the Tsuki-Yomi Scion got his Stars relic as a Trophy? Or maybe, since it's more of a &quot;peacetime&quot; setting, maybe Tsuki-Yomi just traded a god from another pantheon for it? I'll keep working on a more intriguing plot hook, but that may end up being something of a fallback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T10:38:32-08:00","id":38338,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything inherently Titanish about Amatsu-Mikaboshi in legend. He's a very minor figure from what I know. I remember Anne of JSR saying that she thought the only reason he's a Titan is because he's an antagonist in Marvel Comics? Seems like the kinda thing Scion writers might do. They did manage to have the Scion of Set be a snake monster, after all. He could easily be a Minor God among the Kami and perfectly willing to offer up Stars Relics.<br /> <br /> What <i>form</i> those relics might take, though, who knows?! A black jade disc inlaid with silver stars that shifts to reflect the night sky? A magical pearl (always popular) that glows with the power of the morning star? Dunno.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would suggest that since your characters are starting as Demigods, their Relics might be a bit more sophisticated than just 1-dot Purview Keys. Work the Purview-access powers into more interesting Relics with unique powers. The Scion of Ishtar might have a mace that belongs to Erra's Warrior of Fire (check the Poem of Erra for some awesome fun), giving him access to the Fire Purview and also acting as a totally badass weapon. His beard-bling might grant him the power of Health because it used to belong to Tammuz, Ishtar's husband. Maybe the beard-bling includes pieces of the pails that Tammuz used to carry milk to Ishtar as part of his wedding gift and the epic romance imbued into the metal makes him nearly irresistible to women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T12:07:54-08:00","id":38368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions#post38158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Scion is a Scion of Ishtar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That carries some downright unfortunate implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T12:23:50-08:00","id":38376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38368#post38368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That carries some downright unfortunate implications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T16:45:07-08:00","id":38491,"title":"","content":"Warren Beatty and Dustin Hoffman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T17:55:40-08:00","id":38510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions#post38158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second character isn't as bad off. The player has several relic ideas already, but two Purviews escape him right now. He's playing a Scion of Tsuki-Yomi. and the two Purviews with which he's having trouble are Psychopomp and Stars. What would be an appropriate relic(s) for a Japanese Scion with these two powers?<br /> <br /> Also, as we are using Gotham By Night's Stars Purview, he's already noticed that Boon they have where you can call down the constellations to aid you. Does anyone know any books and/or web sites that detail Japanese Astrology? Where can one find information on Japanese constellations?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you go into a bit more detail about who the Scion of Tsuki-yomi is supposed to be and what he does? Perhaps elaborate on what kind of Birthrights he already has in mind?<br /> <br /> Regarding Stars, I'd recommend some kind of Japanese clothing woven by Orihime. She's more interesting than Ama-tsu-mikaboshi because she is more fleshed out. Furthermore, she can be connected to the Chinese shen for inter-pantheon shenanigans, though Orihime and Zhinu are different enough that the pair can also be kept as separate but similar figures. If he wants to relate his usage of the Stars purview to Japanese astrology, other possibilities include but are not limited to the implements used by onmyoji and other Shinto priests. Ofuda seem a bit too ephemeral to me (not to mention cliched), but a ritual baton, a wooden wand, or even a mobile shrine carried in processions might be suited to his tastes.<br /> <br /> If none these options appeal to him, stick a piece of something appropriate in a brocade bag, hang it with a bit of string, and call it an omamori.<br /> <br /> Regarding Psychopomp, it depends on a lot on what he wants to do with the Scion. If he wants to focus on the bit about guiding the souls of the deceased, toss him one of those paper lanterns that can be carried on a stick. Alternatively, if he wants to be a messenger of the gods, I'd recommend a sashimono, which has very strong military implications. Of course, you could also recommend a simple pair of straw sandals, but that strikes me as a bit boring on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T18:20:30-08:00","id":38530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38510#post38510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you go into a bit more detail about who the Scion of Tsuki-yomi is supposed to be and what he does? Perhaps elaborate on what kind of Birthrights he already has in mind?<br /> <br /> Regarding Stars, I'd recommend some kind of Japanese clothing woven by Orihime. She's more interesting than Ama-tsu-mikaboshi because she is more fleshed out. Furthermore, she can be connected to the Chinese shen for inter-pantheon shenanigans, though Orihime and Zhinu are different enough that the pair can also be kept as separate but similar figures. If he wants to relate his usage of the Stars purview to Japanese astrology, other possibilities include but are not limited to the implements used by onmyoji and other Shinto priests. Ofuda seem a bit too ephemeral to me (not to mention cliched), but a ritual baton, a wooden wand, or even a mobile shrine carried in processions might be suited to his tastes.<br /> <br /> If none these options appeal to him, stick a piece of something appropriate in a brocade bag, hang it with a bit of string, and call it an omamori.<br /> <br /> Regarding Psychopomp, it depends on a lot on what he wants to do with the Scion. If he wants to focus on the bit about guiding the souls of the deceased, toss him one of those paper lanterns that can be carried on a stick. Alternatively, if he wants to be a messenger of the gods, I'd recommend a sashimono, which has very strong military implications. Of course, you could also recommend a simple pair of straw sandals, but that strikes me as a bit boring on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, at this point, I don't have much more information on the Tsuki-Yomi Scion. Sadly, this player is notorious for being pretty slow at developing his characters. It took him almost our entire preliminary meeting just to decide he wanted to be a Scion of Tsuki-Yomi and to pick his four specialty Purviews.<br /> <br /> I do know that his relic that allows him to channel both the Water and Moon Purviews is some kind of spear-like weapon deal. I don't know exactly how to describe it, but it's supposed to be a kind of polearm. I'm pretty sure it's his own design. If it was just a naginata, or whatever, he would've just said &quot;It's a naginata.&quot; So I'm guessing it'll be something unique. Now, he just needs to figure out what he wants to do for Stars and Psychopomp.<br /> <br /> Sounds like I'll have to do some research on Orihime. So for an article of clothing designed by her, what would you be thinking about? Some kind of headband? Perhaps a special robe or kimono? The onmyoji implements are intriguing, I can tell him to look into those. The omamori idea has merit as well. I can't believe I didn't think about those, I just got one from a Japanese friend a few months back.<br /> <br /> The sashimono for Psychopomp may be a great idea. I always loved those things. Makes identifying different sides in a samurai battle so much easier. Did sashimono have different markings to denote a soldier's duties? Like was there a sashimono just for &quot;Messenger?&quot; If so, that may be perfect. Heck, if he wants to modernize it a little (not to mention avoiding drawing too much attention if he happens to be walking down Main Street or whatever) he may even consider a tattoo of a &quot;Messenger&quot; sashimono.<br /> <br /> Pretty good suggestions here. I'll pass them on to my player and ask him if he's made any progress on his character's back story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T19:34:06-08:00","id":38542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38530#post38530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, at this point, I don't have much more information on the Tsuki-Yomi Scion. Sadly, this player is notorious for being pretty slow at developing his characters. It took him almost our entire preliminary meeting just to decide he wanted to be a Scion of Tsuki-Yomi and to pick his four specialty Purviews.<br /> <br /> I do know that his relic that allows him to channel both the Water and Moon Purviews is some kind of spear-like weapon deal. I don't know exactly how to describe it, but it's supposed to be a kind of polearm. I'm pretty sure it's his own design. If it was just a naginata, or whatever, he would've just said &quot;It's a naginata.&quot; So I'm guessing it'll be something unique. Now, he just needs to figure out what he wants to do for Stars and Psychopomp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asking for background details sounds out of the question, but do you have any idea if the character is going to specialize in fighting or social skills?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sounds like I'll have to do some research on Orihime. So for an article of clothing designed by her, what would you be thinking about? Some kind of headband? Perhaps a special robe or kimono? The onmyoji implements are intriguing, I can tell him to look into those. The omamori idea has merit as well. I can't believe I didn't think about those, I just got one from a Japanese friend a few months back. </div> </div> </div>Orihime is supposed to be a princess of some kind, but a lot depends on her role in the narrative. I'd recommend a haori, perhaps with a bonus to Appearance to reflect the fact that she is supposed to be a skilled weaver, but some kind of kimono should also be fine if a bit more restrictive. I can't see Orihime making headbands and other minor accessories barring unusual circumstances, but I see no reason that a piece of cloth from one of her creations can't be re-purposed into something along those lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sashimono for Psychopomp may be a great idea. I always loved those things. Makes identifying different sides in a samurai battle so much easier. Did sashimono have different markings to denote a soldier's duties? Like was there a sashimono just for &quot;Messenger?&quot; If so, that may be perfect. Heck, if he wants to modernize it a little (not to mention avoiding drawing too much attention if he happens to be walking down Main Street or whatever) he may even consider a tattoo of a &quot;Messenger&quot; sashimono. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> I believe I recall most sashimono bearing the mon of the clan for ease of identification, but also that some of them had identifiers for the soldier's unit. I'd go with a mon representing either Tsukiyomi or the Scion because he might be important enough for a personal identifier to be recognizable.<br /> <br /> Back tattoos that light up in battle sound cool - perhaps the anima banners of the Exalted could serve as more modern inspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:26:31-08:00","id":38593,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38542#post38542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Asking for background details sounds out of the question, but do you have any idea if the character is going to specialize in fighting or social skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing the player and the story? Probably fighting skills will be primary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38542#post38542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orihime is supposed to be a princess of some kind, but a lot depends on her role in the narrative. I'd recommend a haori, perhaps with a bonus to Appearance to reflect the fact that she is supposed to be a skilled weaver, but some kind of kimono should also be fine if a bit more restrictive. I can't see Orihime making headbands and other minor accessories barring unusual circumstances, but I see no reason that a piece of cloth from one of her creations can't be re-purposed into something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Haori sounds promising. Yeah, a full kimono would be a bit conspicuous in the modern age. Okay, adding that to the list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38542#post38542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> I believe I recall most sashimono bearing the mon of the clan for ease of identification, but also that some of them had identifiers for the soldier's unit. I'd go with a mon representing either Tsukiyomi or the Scion because he might be important enough for a personal identifier to be recognizable.<br /> <br /> Back tattoos that light up in battle sound cool - perhaps the anima banners of the Exalted could serve as more modern inspiration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a Tsuki-Yomi mon would work.<br /> <br /> I think he may like the tattoo idea. And yeah, he's an Exalted fan too, so he might very well look to them for inspiration.<br /> <br /> Definitely getting some good ideas here. I'll be seeing my player tomorrow. I'll see what he thinks about these ideas. I've saved some sample pictures of haori, sashimono, and onmyoji gear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:43:36-08:00","id":38603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38376#post38376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Care to elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Ishtar is the Goddess of Love, Sex, War and Misfortune. The very last one is key here, because anyone who she loves tends to get seriously fucked over.<br /> <br /> Once, she loved the Horse and now we use them as beasts of burden.<br /> Once, she loved the Lion and now we hunt them and wear their skins 'n put them in circuses.<br /> Once she loved Gilgamesh and his best friend executed by way of disease for disrespecting her.<br /> <br /> So, assuming said Scion was <i>not</i> the result of a purely physical fling, that Scion has either seen somethiing awful happen to their mortal parents or is on the verge of seeing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T05:41:46-08:00","id":38690,"title":"","content":"And let us not forget what happens to Tammuz every year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T06:13:14-08:00","id":38696,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly safe to be involved with <i>any</i> deity, so it isn't like Ishtar is especially unique in being a terrible person to get involved with. However, that's probably not especially relevant to the original issue of Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Btw, Unnatural1, were you <i>just</i> looking for Relics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T06:13:39-08:00","id":38697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38603#post38603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Ishtar is the Goddess of Love, Sex, War and Misfortune. The very last one is key here, because anyone who she loves tends to get seriously fucked over.<br /> <br /> Once, she loved the Horse and now we use them as beasts of burden.<br /> Once, she loved the Lion and now we hunt them and wear their skins 'n put them in circuses.<br /> Once she loved Gilgamesh and his best friend executed by way of disease for disrespecting her.<br /> <br /> So, assuming said Scion was <i>not</i> the result of a purely physical fling, that Scion has either seen somethiing awful happen to their mortal parents or is on the verge of seeing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less cryptic than my response, but - This. Things will not end well for this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T08:00:09-08:00","id":38735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38603#post38603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Ishtar is the Goddess of Love, Sex, War and Misfortune. The very last one is key here, because anyone who she loves tends to get seriously fucked over.<br /> <br /> Once, she loved the Horse and now we use them as beasts of burden.<br /> Once, she loved the Lion and now we hunt them and wear their skins 'n put them in circuses.<br /> Once she loved Gilgamesh and his best friend executed by way of disease for disrespecting her.<br /> <br /> So, assuming said Scion was <i>not</i> the result of a purely physical fling, that Scion has either seen somethiing awful happen to their mortal parents or is on the verge of seeing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Yes, that's true I suppose. I guess I should consider that when plotting storylines for the character.<br /> <br /> But as Telgar said, getting involved with any of the gods can be a risky venture. So choosing Ishtar as a divine parent isn't an inherently worse choice than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T08:06:05-08:00","id":38737,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38696#post38696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not exactly safe to be involved with <i>any</i> deity, so it isn't like Ishtar is especially unique in being a terrible person to get involved with. However, that's probably not especially relevant to the original issue of Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Btw, Unnatural1, were you <i>just</i> looking for Relics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very true.<br /> <br /> <br /> And no, I'm not only looking for Relics. In general, the character has ten dots worth of Birthrights to pick out, so nothing is really out of the question. In fact, I was just looking through the Annuna download from Gotham By Night and I just noticed their writeup for Zu birds as a Creature. Giant hawks with the fangs and claws of lions that you can ride? Now THAT sounds kinda badass.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you've got any Creatures, Followers, Guides or whatnot, the more options the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T09:01:58-08:00","id":38756,"title":"","content":"Your Sumerian might enjoy griffons, sphinxes, manticores or sirrushes (mushussus) as Creatures. Lamastu could be fun as either a Guide or Follower (Followers?). Mesopotamia is lousy with mythological beings and minor deities. Depending on how well this PC gets along with Nergal (also called Erra), one of the Seven Warriors might be an awesome Guide for him: Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Venom, Beast and Fear. <br /> <br /> If your Kami dude is having trouble coming up with <i>Relics</i> to access his Purviews, about about rolling his Purview Keys into Creatures? He could have a pet tanuki or something that grants him Psychopomp with its wandering ways. Even a lesser kami of stars that grants him Stars while it follows him around, doing little star-kami things. Glowing, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T09:47:28-08:00","id":38769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38756#post38756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Sumerian might enjoy griffons, sphinxes, manticores or sirrushes (mushussus) as Creatures. Lamastu could be fun as either a Guide or Follower (Followers?). Mesopotamia is lousy with mythological beings and minor deities. Depending on how well this PC gets along with Nergal (also called Erra), one of the Seven Warriors might be an awesome Guide for him: Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Venom, Beast and Fear.<br /> <br /> If your Kami dude is having trouble coming up with <i>Relics</i> to access his Purviews, about about rolling his Purview Keys into Creatures? He could have a pet tanuki or something that grants him Psychopomp with its wandering ways. Even a lesser kami of stars that grants him Stars while it follows him around, doing little star-kami things. Glowing, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just got done researching the Seven Warriors, and yeah, one of those guys would be a BADASS Guide. Probably Fire, since the Ishtar Scion intends to specialize in the Fire Purview. As I said, the Zu birds in the Annuna download are also quite impressive.<br /> <br /> I did some research on Lamashtu, and I'm not sure how great a Guide or Follower she'd be. Unless my research is incomplete? I know Lamashtu is one of the precursors to the myth of Lilith. Your mention that there may be more than one is intriguing. Is there a case for there being a race of Lamashtu created by her? Giving this guy a succubus-like Follower(s) might be interesting.<br /> <br /> The Creature idea for the Kami Scion has definite merit. Tanuki are kinda cool. And yeah, the Kami have a practically built-in &quot;instant Guide/Follower&quot; system with their whole &quot;Everything has a Kami attached to it&quot; mentality. I don't need a myth to support the kami's existence. Japanese Mythology doesn't cover even a small fraction of the number of Kami in the World. Just dream up one &quot;Kami of the Stars&quot; and Presto! Instant Guide. I'm definitely adding that one to the list for my Kami player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:02:38-08:00","id":38772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38769#post38769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Creature idea for the Kami Scion has definite merit. Tanuki are kinda cool. And yeah, the Kami have a practically built-in &quot;instant Guide/Follower&quot; system with their whole &quot;Everything has a Kami attached to it&quot; mentality. I don't need a myth to support the kami's existence. Japanese Mythology doesn't cover even a small fraction of the number of Kami in the World. Just dream up one &quot;Kami of the Stars&quot; and Presto! Instant Guide. I'm definitely adding that one to the list for my Kami player.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend a chochinobake for Psychopomp, which is a paper lantern tsukumogami.<br /> <br /> That said, you're absolutely right about Japanese Scions having lots of options for Guides and Followers, though I'd recommend avoiding anything too closely tied to death, disease, and disaster. Unless you want to go with a story about the Scion challenging the established beliefs of his pantheon, which can be interesting in its own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:52:10-08:00","id":38791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38772#post38772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd recommend a chochinobake for Psychopomp, which is a paper lantern tsukumogami.<br /> <br /> That said, you're absolutely right about Japanese Scions having lots of options for Guides and Followers, though I'd recommend avoiding anything too closely tied to death, disease, and disaster. Unless you want to go with a story about the Scion challenging the established beliefs of his pantheon, which can be interesting in its own way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chochinobake are also pretty interesting. And yeah, sounds like they'd be perfect for the whole &quot;Guiding the dead&quot; aspect of Psychopomp.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I don't think the player is interested in getting into death, disease, and disaster. I mean, with the Water Purview, he can certainly cause death and disaster, but I doubt that'll be a central theme for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T10:53:44-08:00","id":38792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=38769#post38769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did some research on Lamashtu, and I'm not sure how great a Guide or Follower she'd be. Unless my research is incomplete? I know Lamashtu is one of the precursors to the myth of Lilith. Your mention that there may be more than one is intriguing. Is there a case for there being a race of Lamashtu created by her? Giving this guy a succubus-like Follower(s) might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, one of the cool things about Scion is that it gives you a lot of freedom in how you interprit and represent myth. In Babylonian myth, there is just one Lamastu, a singular demonic being. However, there's no reason that she can't be a Titanspawn or lesser Goddess that <i>has</i> spawned a race of succubus-like followers! I had a Scion of Nergal as a PC in my last Scion game for a while. He had a powerful Lamastu as a follower and seemed to quite enjoy her, even if she was occasionally prone to eating people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T22:17:13-08:00","id":39144,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I met with both of my friends who are playing the Ishtar and Tsuki-Yomi Scions. We haven't completely ironed out everything, but some progress has been made.<br /> <br /> For the Ishtar Scion? Telgar, you'll be happy to know that he loved the idea of the beard bling for his Health relics. He's not certain he plans to do the whole &quot;Babylonian goat beard&quot; look just yet, but he said even if he decides to go clean-shaven, those beard ornaments would work just as well in one's hair if it's long enough. But one way or the other, he thinks the beard bling idea is really cool. Especially the idea of it being made from the same milk pails Tammuz brought to Ishtar.<br /> <br /> As for the Fire Purview? He's thinking he may not even NEED a relic in the strictest sense. He is thinking about using the Me Purview for his Fire Boons. The first dot of Me, of course, makes it possible to wield the given Purview without the need for a relic. Failing that? He is considering letting his Fire relic be a weapon. He's definitely intrigued by the Babylonian mace designs we looked up, so he's thinkin about a mace. On the other hand, he pointed out that a mace seems to suggest &quot;Earth&quot; rather than &quot;Fire&quot; to him. To that end, he looked into some Mesopotamian sword designs and he was quite intrigued that the Mesopotamians also used a sword very similar to the khopesh. So he's considering that as well.<br /> <br /> For Illusion? He's still not quite sure. He's considering just going with a ring or something. More information is needed.<br /> <br /> For Chaos? He's thinking about either another ring, or perhaps some kind of amulet.<br /> <br /> As far as Creatures or Guides or Followers? He was very intrigued by the Zu bird. He was also quite intrigued by the Lamashtu concept. The idea of having his own pet succubus is definitely interesting to him.<br /> <br /> For the Tsuki-Yomi Scion? As usual, this player is waffling a bit. He's now considering switching to the Celestial Bureaucracy and going with Nuwa (she also has a lot of the powers he's looking for.) Nonetheless, he did discover that the Japanese pretty much use the same Astrology system as the Chinese, so for his Stars relic, he's considering going with this really cool feng shui compass he found online. He thinks it may even serve as his Psychopomp relic as well.<br /> <br /> So that's pretty much the latest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T22:34:41-08:00","id":39156,"title":"","content":"Very cool. Yes, Beard Bling would work just as well in your hair most of the time. He could wear it however he wants, really. Scions don't have to mimic ancient styles, they can put their own modern twist on them.<br /> <br /> For Illusion and Chaos, if he's really stumped, he could just resort to the classic Babylonian standbys: Cuneiform Tablets and Cylinder Seals. Rings aren't bad, but tablets and seals really project 'Babylon'. Or, if he decides to go with a Lamastu Follower, she could act as his access key for Chaos. They're very Chaotic creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T23:44:35-08:00","id":39197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/38158-seeking-some-birthright-suggestions?p=39156#post39156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very cool. Yes, Beard Bling would work just as well in your hair most of the time. He could wear it however he wants, really. Scions don't have to mimic ancient styles, they can put their own modern twist on them.<br /> <br /> For Illusion and Chaos, if he's really stumped, he could just resort to the classic Babylonian standbys: Cuneiform Tablets and Cylinder Seals. Rings aren't bad, but tablets and seals really project 'Babylon'. Or, if he decides to go with a Lamastu Follower, she could act as his access key for Chaos. They're very Chaotic creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm starting to think that a cuneiform tablet could be really cool for Chaos and/or Illusion. It'll be up to my player, of course, but a tablet is relatively easy to carry, and couldn't be more Babylonian if it tried.<br /> <br /> Cylinder Seals? I'm suddenly thinking that it could be useful with Illusion. I mean, their whole point was to roll out an image on to clay. I just had this great idea of a cylinder seal that actually changes it's images to actually reflect the illusions the Scion may be conjuring somehow. Gives a nice flair of authenticity to the idea of magic wielded by the Babylonian Gods. It certainly beats the idea of just carrying around a big stone cylinder that doesn't seem to do anything.<br /> <br /> Channeling Chaos through a Lamashtu also sounds intriguing. That may be a big selling point on getting the player to take this option. He was already intrigued. Perhaps that may convince him completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T03:38:39-08:00","id":39289,"title":"","content":"My only caveat to players with regards to weapon relics is that they need to remember those are going to be the first things someone tries to take away from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:35:04-08:00","id":43699,"title":"","content":"Okay, we're getting ever closer to having these two characters fully fleshed out. I'll post the full information about them once we've finalized everything.<br /> <br /> Right now, the Ishtar player has one question about the beard bling/hair accessories he's using for his Health Boons. He likes Telgar's idea that they're made from one of the milk pails that Tammuz brought to Ishtar as a wedding gift.<br /> <br /> Telgar, you mentioned that having Relics tied to such an epic romance may give him some kind of &quot;irresistible to women&quot; affect? We were wondering how to stat that up as a Birthright? I'm thinking that it's basically an &quot;Always On&quot; version of the Epic Manipulation Knack &quot;Seductive Mien?&quot; For those of you who aren't familiar? Seductive Mien can be found on the Gotham By Night site. It's a Knack that makes you able to seduce basically anyone regardless of their preferences. It has no pre-requisites and only costs one Legend.<br /> <br /> If that's not how to go, does anyone have any better ideas on how to stat such and effect as a Birthright? Is that just one extra dot or should such a powerful effect cost more Birthright dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:42:31-08:00","id":43706,"title":"","content":"It depends on the value assigned to such a trait. At low levels, it might just be a small bonus to Charisma and/or Appearance rolls related to seduction. At higher levels, it could be automatic successes or even make it require an effort of will on the part of any interested party <i>not</i> to attempt to sleep with him. That'd get him in a lot of trouble, but then gifts from Ishtar probably do that a lot anyway.<br /> <br /> The precise effect would depend highly on how your game specifically handles social effects. That's something that varies wildly between all games, so I can't provide a blanket answer. The safest, easiest way to represent such a power is just the bonus to his Seduction rolls. You could also modify Seductive Mein, as you noted. Simply give him the once-per-day Super Seduction effect, or remove all external penalties from his normal seduction rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:52:28-08:00","id":43710,"title":"","content":"Okay, so giving him some bonus dice to seduction rolls would be kinda Hero-level. Auto-Successes would be more like Demigod-level?<br /> <br /> The once-per-day Super Seduction effect sounds like it may work as well. Just the idea of an almost guaranteed seduction success can be a big advantage for a character like this. This would also force him to actually BUY the Seductive Mien Knack instead of just relying on his relics to do the job for him. He can use Seductive Mien as normal any time, but once a day, he has the option of an almost foolproof seduction. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> The idea of an effect that makes people/things have to try to NOT try to sleep with him has appeal too. As you say, that leads to all kinds of troubling circumstances that can arise. Him running afoul of a large group of Amazons with those things on just seems all kind of entertaining! Or worse yet? A giantess notices him and doesn't feel like spending a Willpower? &quot;Snu-snu,&quot; anybody?<br /> <br /> Okay, the Super Seduction effect sounds like it may be a what? Two-dot power? Maybe three? The &quot;Spend Willpower to NOT want him&quot; effect would be about the same? What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:07:39-08:00","id":43720,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, these dot ratings are based on what I would peg them at, and I tend to be pretty generous with Relic powers, but less generous with dice-adding effects because I think dice-effects are the root of many problems in Scion's system. They're simple, easy and they get out of hand <i>really fast</i>. <br /> <br /> +Legend (a useful rating, since it scales and never becomes <i>entirely </i>useless) dice to his seduction rolls is probably 2 dots. The same in autos would be 4.<br /> <br /> A once/day Super Seduction effect would be 3 dots.<br /> <br /> A constant Sexy Aura that requires anyone affected (which could be anyone, or anyone of his Legend or lower, or anyone at his Legend +2 or lower... it depends how you want to run that) to spend a WP per scene not to want to jump his bones (until some limit is reached to avoid having party members and friendly NPCs constantly affected) would be a dramatically game-influencing power. 4-5 dots, depending on the limits and how severely negative the consequences can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:16:27-08:00","id":43722,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think your breakdown seems about right to me.<br /> <br /> I'll pass this on to my player and let him think about how many Birthright dots he wants to commit to this. If I know him, I'm pretty sure he'll take either Super Seduction or the Sexy Aura, but he has surprised me in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T15:01:10-08:00","id":44463,"title":"","content":"Okay, just heard back from my Ishtar player.<br /> <br /> He thinks he'll take the Super Seduction effect. Indeed, our conversation about this effect led to a new line of discussion that I may open a new thread to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}